====Usage notes====
Although ''a'' {{m|en||decade}} may refer to any group of ten years, it often particularly refers to the informal ten-year periods of the calendar whose last digits run from 0 to 9. Some style guides may prefer that ''decade'' refers exclusively to such calendar periods while {{m|en|decennium}}, {{m|en|decennary}}, etc. refers to ten-year periods in other contexts. Similarly, a {{m|en|quinquennium}} etc. may be any five-year period, whereas {{m|en|pentad}} and {{m|en|quintade}} are used for the two halves of a calendrical decade.

It should be noted that the method of computing a decade is distinguished from the proper computation of {{m|en|century|centuries}} and {{m|en|millennium|millennia}}, which run from 1 to 0. The 1st century began with the year 1 and ended with the year 100, but "the [[Nineties]]" are the years whose name includes the word {{m|en|ninety}}, from '90 to '99, all the years of a century with a 9 as their tens place digit.

